# What a `docker build` with modules/documents as its context must not send. Both the Docling
# image (processing/Dockerfile) and the generation worker (generation/worker/Dockerfile) build
# from here, so they can take the shared helpers in utils/.
#
# Keep this and .maven-dockerignore identical: the Maven one is read only by the fabric8
# docker-maven-plugin, this one only by plain `docker build`, and nothing checks that they agree.
# Both Dockerfiles COPY named directories, so this keeps the context small (processing's .venv
# alone is ~100 MB) and keeps stale bytecode out of the images.
api/
**/target/
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/src/test/
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
